WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.248
Myelodysplastic syndromes, or MDS,

00:00:02.298 --> 00:00:06.235
are a group of cancers in which immature blood cells in the

00:00:06.285 --> 00:00:09.681
bone marrow do not mature into healthy blood cells.

00:00:09.731 --> 00:00:14.222
Normally, blood stem cells in the marrow develop into red blood cells,

00:00:14.272 --> 00:00:16.362
white blood cells, and platelets.

00:00:16.412 --> 00:00:21.247
In MDS, the cells are poorly formed or do not work properly.

00:00:21.297 --> 00:00:25.101
They die in the marrow or soon after entering the bloodstream,

00:00:25.151 --> 00:00:28.892
and over time the defective cells outnumber the healthy ones.

00:00:28.942 --> 00:00:33.024
The result is low blood counts, called cytopenias.

00:00:33.074 --> 00:00:36.519
MDS is mainly a disease of older adults.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:42.196
The median age at diagnosis is about 70, and it is uncommon before age 50.

00:00:42.246 --> 00:00:47.164
The American Cancer Society says the exact number of new cases is not known,

00:00:47.214 --> 00:00:51.870
but some estimates start at about 10,000 each year in the United States.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:55.938
Most cases of MDS have no known cause.

00:00:55.988 --> 00:01:01.191
Known risk factors include previous chemotherapy or radiation therapy for cancer,

00:01:01.241 --> 00:01:05.666
and exposure to chemicals such as benzene, tobacco smoke, pesticides,

00:01:05.716 --> 00:01:08.325
and heavy metals such as lead or mercury.

00:01:08.375 --> 00:01:11.055
Early on, MDS often causes no symptoms,

00:01:11.105 --> 00:01:14.205
and it may be found on a routine blood count.

00:01:14.255 --> 00:01:17.642
When symptoms do appear, they follow the low counts.

00:01:17.692 --> 00:01:23.658
Low red blood cells, called anemia, cause fatigue, weakness, shortness of breath,

00:01:23.708 --> 00:01:24.698
and pale skin.

00:01:24.748 --> 00:01:27.664
Low platelets cause easy bruising or bleeding,

00:01:27.714 --> 00:01:31.597
and tiny red or purple spots under the skin called petechiae.

00:01:31.647 --> 00:01:35.018
Low white blood cells lead to frequent infections.

00:01:35.068 --> 00:01:38.488
Anemia is a central feature of several MDS subtypes,

00:01:38.538 --> 00:01:41.090
so treating it is a major part of care.

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:44.729
Diagnosis begins with a complete blood count with

00:01:44.779 --> 00:01:47.162
differential and a peripheral blood smear,

00:01:47.212 --> 00:01:50.986
along with blood chemistry studies such as vitamin B12 and folate.

00:01:51.036 --> 00:01:54.701
It also requires a bone marrow aspiration and biopsy.

00:01:54.751 --> 00:01:58.740
The marrow is examined for abnormal looking cells, called dysplasia,

00:01:58.790 --> 00:02:02.481
and for the percentage of blasts, which are the youngest cells.

00:02:02.531 --> 00:02:05.435
Further laboratory tests on the marrow include

00:02:05.485 --> 00:02:08.004
flow cytometry and cytogenetic analysis,

00:02:08.054 --> 00:02:12.884
which looks for chromosome changes, such as a missing piece of chromosome 5,

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:13.783
called del 5q.

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:17.063
Newer testing also looks for gene mutations.

00:02:17.113 --> 00:02:20.881
Subtypes are defined by which blood cell lines are affected,

00:02:20.931 --> 00:02:25.145
whether ring sideroblasts are present, whether del 5q occurs alone,

00:02:25.195 --> 00:02:26.990
and the percentage of blasts.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.924
Doctors estimate prognosis with scoring systems.

00:02:30.974 --> 00:02:35.150
The Revised International Prognostic Scoring System, or IPSS-R,

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.780
uses the percentage of blasts in the bone marrow, chromosome changes,

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:43.805
and the depth of anemia, low platelets, and low neutrophils.

00:02:43.855 --> 00:02:50.521
It places patients in five categories: very low, low, intermediate, high,

00:02:50.571 --> 00:02:51.809
and very high.

00:02:51.859 --> 00:02:55.182
Very low and low are generally called lower risk,

00:02:55.232 --> 00:02:58.348
and high and very high are called higher risk.

00:02:58.398 --> 00:03:02.206
The newer IPSS-M adds mutation testing.

00:03:02.256 --> 00:03:05.775
It was built by profiling 152 genes in nearly 3,000 patients,

00:03:05.825 --> 00:03:07.824
and it defines six risk categories.

00:03:07.874 --> 00:03:12.669
It improved prognostic discrimination compared with IPSS-R,

00:03:12.719 --> 00:03:17.514
and it changed the risk grouping of 46 percent of patients.

00:03:17.565 --> 00:03:20.828
The MDS Foundation estimates that roughly 30 percent of

00:03:20.878 --> 00:03:23.780
patients will progress to acute myeloid leukemia.

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:27.818
Treatment depends on risk category and symptoms.

00:03:27.868 --> 00:03:32.550
Supportive care is the foundation: transfusions of red cells or platelets,

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:37.923
antibiotics for infections, and iron chelation when transfusions cause iron buildup.

00:03:37.973 --> 00:03:41.818
Erythropoiesis stimulating agents may improve anemia.

00:03:41.868 --> 00:03:44.070
For lower risk disease with anemia,

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:48.702
options include lenalidomide for patients with del 5q, and luspatercept,

00:03:48.752 --> 00:03:51.919
which the FDA approved for adults with very low to

00:03:51.969 --> 00:03:55.715
intermediate risk MDS who may require regular transfusions,

00:03:55.765 --> 00:04:00.219
including those who have not used an erythropoiesis stimulating agent.

00:04:00.269 --> 00:04:01.249
In June 2024,

00:04:01.299 --> 00:04:05.451
the FDA approved imetelstat for low to intermediate 1

00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:08.860
risk MDS with transfusion dependent anemia.

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:10.312
In the IMerge trial,

00:04:10.362 --> 00:04:16.048
39.8 percent of imetelstat patients went at least 8 weeks without transfusions,

00:04:16.098 --> 00:04:18.661
compared with 15 percent on placebo.

00:04:18.711 --> 00:04:23.451
In higher risk disease, azacitidine has been shown to improve survival.

00:04:23.501 --> 00:04:28.338
Allogeneic stem cell transplant is the only potentially curative treatment.

00:04:28.388 --> 00:04:29.810
Thank you for watching.
